1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,086
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,554
[Ria] <i>Ma'am, I'm sorry,</i>
<i>but we aren't allowed</i>

3
00:00:12,637 --> 00:00:14,431
<i>to accept any visitors at the moment.</i>

4
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:16,099
<i>We aren't your typical guests.</i>

5
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:17,642
<i>This is a courtesy call from the mayor.</i>

6
00:00:17,726 --> 00:00:20,603
[Emilia] <i>And the former governor</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

7
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:23,690
<i>I need a huge sum of money</i>
<i>to get back into power</i>

8
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:27,861
<i>and stop my enemies' plans against me.</i>

9
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:29,487
<i>Like this one person.</i>

10
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:31,114
<i>I don't know if you're familiar with her.</i>

11
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:31,990
<i>Camia Cruz?</i>

12
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:33,366
[Ivy] <i>Doesn't ring a bell.</i>

13
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:37,537
[Julio] <i>The moment you got your own land,</i>

14
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,623
<i>you thought you could live</i>
<i>by your own rules.</i>

15
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:45,044
<i>Therefore, I'll make you feel</i>
<i>what it's like to own land</i>

16
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,088
<i>without the government's support.</i>

17
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,299
<i>-Where's my mother?</i>
<i>-Emilia had her killed.</i>

18
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:51,801
[Diego] <i>They killed my mother!</i>
<i>Where's the justice?!</i>

19
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:53,720
<i>-The Ardientes will kill you…</i>
<i>-Pandoy!</i>

20
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,597
<i>…if you go against them!</i>

21
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:58,516
[Ivy] <i>Mom, I agreed to do the procedure.</i>

22
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,771
<i>Just like what Dad said, learn to fight.</i>

23
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:06,066
<i>Learn to take risks.</i>
<i>And learn to have faith.</i>

24
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:09,652
<i>-Lily, my daughter.</i>
<i>-You remember me now.</i>

25
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:11,905
<i>You remember me!</i>

26
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,365
<i>Lily, I remember everything now.</i>

27
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:18,244
<i>I want to know what happened</i>
<i>after your father and I lost you.</i>

28
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:20,705
<i>I want to visit your father's grave.</i>

29
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:23,666
<i>Mom, for now, this ring will have to do</i>

30
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:27,921
<i>because I can't let you go back</i>
<i>to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

31
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:30,215
<i>You and Mom will go</i>
<i>to our house in Manila.</i>

32
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:32,258
<i>What about you? Aren't you coming too?</i>

33
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,636
<i>I have to fulfill my promise to the people</i>

34
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:35,929
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

35
00:01:36,012 --> 00:01:39,057
<i>And I still have to seek justice</i>
<i>for my father's death.</i>

36
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,100
[Diego] <i>Please forgive me</i>
<i>for what I'm about to do.</i>

37
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:42,519
<i>I will never have peace</i>

38
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:45,730
<i>until I confront the people</i>
<i>who murdered my mother.</i>

39
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:50,527
Sir Diego.

40
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,612
[tense music playing]

41
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:57,784
Stay alert.

42
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:02,122
Make sure you give this all to Papa.

43
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:05,416
And tell him that I still support him

44
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,127
despite what he did to me.

45
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:09,170
Don't forget to give him
all of that, okay?

46
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:10,380
Yes, ma'am.

47
00:02:11,464 --> 00:02:13,508
You're such a good actress.

48
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:16,886
What are you doing here?
We kicked you out, right?

49
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,304
Tell me the truth.

50
00:02:20,431 --> 00:02:21,975
Did you have my real mother killed?

51
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:24,352
[tense music playing]

52
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:42,287
Carlotta?

53
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:53,131
I'm worried about Lily.

54
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:57,427
Why isn't she coming with us?

55
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:01,764
What is my daughter planning to do?

56
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:08,021
Lily's house in Manila is really nice.

57
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,107
It has a peaceful garden too.

58
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:14,611
And if you get bored, the mall
is just 10 minutes away.

59
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:24,454
Carlotta, you're like a mother
to Lily too.

60
00:03:24,996 --> 00:03:28,249
You know how I feel as her mother.

61
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:31,377
Please be honest with me. Woman to woman.

62
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:35,882
What is my daughter planning to do?

63
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:46,601
Camia, I treated Ivy--

64
00:03:47,852 --> 00:03:50,271
I mean, Lily, like my own daughter.

65
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:56,110
And like you, I love her very
much. Even if we aren't related.

66
00:03:57,153 --> 00:04:02,116
And as her foster mother,
I know that no matter what I do,

67
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:09,123
she will find a way to give her
family the justice they deserve.

68
00:04:15,546 --> 00:04:18,174
-Thank you, Carlotta.
-No worries.

69
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:19,384
Thank you.

70
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:29,143
-How dare you?
-Did you have my mother killed?

71
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,814
Answer me. Answer me!

72
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:36,526
Honestly, I don't remember.

73
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:39,445
And, frankly, I don't care
if your mother died.

74
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,322
And, besides… You know? She deserves it.

75
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:42,490
Your mom was a slut.

76
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:43,741
-You murderer!
-Sir!

77
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:45,201
[screams] What are you going to do?!

78
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:49,289
-Sir Diego.
-Jepoy… Jepoy, let me go.

79
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:50,790
I can't let the governor get hurt.

80
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,418
[grunts]

81
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:57,714
Diego, stop it!
You're causing trouble again!

82
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:01,009
Stop it! Diego, enough! Guards! Guards!

83
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:02,135
[screams]

84
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:04,095
Get back!

85
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:12,186
Diego!

86
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,522
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!
-What are you doing?!

87
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:17,984
[Diego grunts]

88
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:21,988
-[Emilia] Stop it! Stop it!
-[grunting]

89
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:24,115
[Arnaldo] You bastard! I'll kill you!

90
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:26,701
[grunts]

91
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:31,622
[Arnaldo screams]

92
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:41,257
[grunting]

93
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:44,552
Sir Diego!

94
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,679
[Emilia] Diego!

95
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:49,182
[coughs]

96
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:54,020
Congressman, Diego's inside.

97
00:05:56,814 --> 00:05:58,357
You ungrateful bastard!

98
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:00,735
This family raised you,
and this is how you repay us?!

99
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,528
[screams]

100
00:06:06,532 --> 00:06:07,533
Arnaldo!

101
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:10,536
That's enough.

102
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,746
He started it!

103
00:06:11,996 --> 00:06:15,333
Papa, he's accusing me
of killing his mother!

104
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:20,671
Why am I not surprised to hear that?

105
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:30,431
I'm glad to know that you have
some guts now, Diego.

106
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:35,478
But you're still an idiot.
Didn't it cross your mind

107
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:38,064
you could've gotten yourself
killed doing this?

108
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:39,816
Now listen.

109
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:44,487
Whatever it is you found out
about your mother…

110
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:48,241
you will keep quiet about it.
Do you understand?

111
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:53,996
Because I don't want
any insignificant matters

112
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,665
to add to my problems.

113
00:06:56,124 --> 00:07:00,586
The best thing for you to do is
to apologize to your mother…

114
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:04,549
and to your brother
for the trouble you've caused.

115
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,927
You're a family of murderers.

116
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:11,139
You're all monsters!

117
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:20,940
[dramatic music playing]

118
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:26,070
Go ahead, Grandpa.

119
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:28,781
[tense music playing]

120
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,408
I'm not afraid to die.

121
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:33,161
I'm not afraid to die!

122
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,122
Do it!

123
00:07:37,623 --> 00:07:38,916
Do it now!

124
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:42,211
[tense music playing]

125
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:46,757
[breathing heavily]

126
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:55,975
If you aren't afraid to die,
then I won't kill you just yet.

127
00:07:57,602 --> 00:08:02,857
But I'll make you feel just
how much you deserve to suffer.

128
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:07,236
Take him outside!

129
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,573
[suspenseful music playing]

130
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:17,997
-Stop it!
-You bastard! You bastard!

131
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:23,377
You're all animals!
You'll pay. You'll all pay!

132
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:34,722
-Have they left yet?
-Not yet.

133
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:36,140
Miss Camia's over there.

134
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:44,565
Mom. What are you still doing here?

135
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:46,442
You'll get stuck in traffic.

136
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:52,448
Lily, I'm not going anywhere.

137
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:56,077
I won't live in Manila.

138
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:01,958
If you're going to fight the Ardientes…

139
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:06,796
then I won't let you go alone.
I'll fight with you.

140
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:10,341
Mom, who told you that?

141
00:09:11,175 --> 00:09:14,720
Carlotta told me all about your
plans against the Ardientes.

142
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:21,269
-Nanny Carlotta!
-Lily… Dear!

143
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,479
Don't blame her.

144
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:25,898
She's only thinking of your safety.

145
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,608
Nanny Carlotta!

146
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:33,698
Lily, you can't force me
to change my mind.

147
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:39,453
If you want to exact revenge on
the Ardientes, I will help you.

148
00:09:57,305 --> 00:10:00,224
[foreboding music playing]

149
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:03,185
Go ahead. Tie him up!

150
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:05,980
[foreboding music continues playing]

151
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:15,281
[groaning]

152
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:22,288
All right. Let's see how tough you are.

153
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,875
[vehicle engine turns over]

154
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,797
[Raul] Diego! Diego!

155
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:34,216
Diego-- Papa! Papa!

156
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:35,968
Papa!

157
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:38,429
-Now drive!
-Papa!

158
00:10:38,512 --> 00:10:40,306
What are you doing to my son?

159
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:44,769
Papa! What are you doing to Diego?!

160
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:49,690
Papa, let him go!
Emilia! What are you doing?

161
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:51,859
Arnaldo, help your brother.

162
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:55,321
Papa, I'm begging you. Please.

163
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:56,530
I'll take his place!

164
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:58,741
Diego!

165
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:14,048
[grunts]

166
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:15,966
-Diego!
-Let him go!

167
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,468
[Raul] Diego!

168
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:20,054
-Raul!
-Let vermin chase vermin!

169
00:11:20,554 --> 00:11:23,808
-Diego! Diego!
-[screaming]

170
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:26,018
-Raul!
-Why, Emilia?

171
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,813
You want to join your husband in hell?

172
00:11:30,272 --> 00:11:32,358
-[Raul] Diego!
-I thought so.

173
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:34,902
-[Raul] Diego! Diego!
-[Diego screams]

174
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:38,280
-[Diego screams]
-Diego!

175
00:11:39,782 --> 00:11:40,825
[grunts]

176
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:55,840
Diego. Diego! Diego, son.

177
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:59,718
-[Diego groaning]
-Hold on. I'll get you free.

178
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,888
-Diego, son.
-[Diego wailing]

179
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:05,891
-Diego.
-[groaning]

180
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:07,685
-Dad…
-Animals!

181
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:08,936
Dad…

182
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:11,313
[Raul] Monsters!

183
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:15,943
I'm here. I'm sorry… I'm here for you.

184
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:19,697
I couldn't… I couldn't…

185
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:26,120
[dramatic music playing]

186
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:34,086
-I'm here now… I'm here now.
-[Diego wailing]

187
00:12:35,629 --> 00:12:37,590
I won't change my mind.

188
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:40,342
You have to, Mom.

189
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:41,677
I'm your mother.

190
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:46,765
You can't just tell me
what I can and cannot do.

191
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:51,562
You don't know what you're
talking about, Mom.

192
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:55,191
You don't know what
the Ardientes are capable of!

193
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:59,403
Yes, I do. I know them inside out!

194
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:03,532
They killed my husband, your father.

195
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:06,160
They took advantage of me!

196
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:09,747
They tore our family apart.

197
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:14,043
If there's someone who'll get revenge,

198
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:16,128
it's me because I'm your mother.

199
00:13:17,254 --> 00:13:20,508
I'm sorry, Mom. But I'll do it alone.

200
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:22,092
I don't want you to get hurt.

201
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:25,930
Lily, I'm sick of hiding.

202
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:28,807
I'm tired of being a ghost.

203
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:33,729
You don't know how much it hurts
not being able

204
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:37,149
to visit your father's grave
because you're hiding me away.

205
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:39,485
-Mom!
-Let me do this.

206
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:41,946
Let me fight for our family too.

207
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:44,990
Let me fight for you.

208
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:48,202
Let me give justice
to your father's death.

209
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:51,747
You're not the only one who lost someone.

210
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,166
I lost my husband.

211
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:59,171
I'm ready to face the Ardientes.

212
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:02,675
I'll make them pay.

213
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:10,224
Both of us, Lily, we'll both get revenge.

214
00:14:10,599 --> 00:14:12,518
[tense music playing]

215
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:18,941
Mom.

216
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:21,569
[soft music playing]

217
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:22,695
[sighs]

218
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,950
This is hard for me, Mom. I can't?

219
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:29,910
I don't want to do this.

220
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:34,123
But for you, I will.

221
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,668
There's only one thing I ask of you.

222
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:43,173
All your decisions, everything
you do, has to go through me.

223
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:50,973
At all times, by any means,
you have to protect yourself.

224
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:52,850
Lily, I'm your mother.

225
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:56,145
I should be the one telling you this.

226
00:14:56,937 --> 00:15:01,025
I know, Mom. I know you're my mother.

227
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:04,945
But there comes a time in every family…

228
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:12,828
when it's the kids' turn to look
after and protect our parents.

229
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:18,667
[sighs] Lily, you don't have to
take care of me.

230
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:20,169
I know, Mom.

231
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,964
But I love you so much.

232
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:28,469
I'm doing this because
I don't want to lose you.

233
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:31,597
I don't want to lose you again.

234
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,391
I can't, Mom.

235
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,114
[Raul] Loring!

236
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:51,575
Loring!

237
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:53,619
Hold on, son.

238
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:57,414
Just a bit more, Diego.
We're already here. Loring!

239
00:15:57,748 --> 00:16:00,125
-Diego!
-Son.

240
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:01,210
-Diego.
-Son.

241
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:02,878
What happened to Diego?!

242
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:06,465
What happened to him?

243
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:09,176
I knew this was going to happen!

244
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:11,679
-Son?
-What did you do to him?!

245
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:14,473
-Son!
-What did you do to Diego?!

246
00:16:14,556 --> 00:16:18,602
-Son! Son, we're here.
-[Loring wails]

247
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:21,981
Why did you take your son home like this?

248
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:26,944
How could you let this
happen to your son?!

249
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,822
[Loring crying]

250
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:35,285
You're a useless father, Raul!

251
00:16:38,163 --> 00:16:41,458
Diego. I'll come back for you, son.

252
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:42,960
I'll come back for you.

253
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:55,222
[Loring] Let go of Diego. Leave!

254
00:16:57,975 --> 00:17:00,561
[wailing]

255
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:12,197
My informer told me the police
are monitoring

256
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:14,033
my gambling den in town.

257
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:16,452
Can't we do something
about this, Congressman?

258
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:18,287
Governor?

259
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:19,997
I'll talk to the police chief tomorrow.

260
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:22,791
And remind him that I line his pockets

261
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:25,544
with thousands every month.

262
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:28,547
Get him to control his people.

263
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:30,758
Okay.

264
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:33,677
Papa. You monster.

265
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:37,264
What did you do to my son?
Why did you do that to him?

266
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:40,017
And you, Arnaldo? Why didn't you stop him?

267
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:42,978
Why did you take my son and not me?!

268
00:17:43,562 --> 00:17:44,521
Why?!

269
00:17:44,605 --> 00:17:46,857
Are you scared of me? Are you a coward?

270
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:49,985
Let him go.

271
00:17:50,819 --> 00:17:51,862
You're a coward--

272
00:17:51,945 --> 00:17:53,614
-That's enough.
-Wait, Arnaldo. Don't--

273
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:54,948
That's enough.

274
00:17:59,661 --> 00:18:03,832
Even your own son doesn't
respect you as a father.

275
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:08,087
Raul, do you know why you're still alive?

276
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:11,507
Because of my debt of gratitude
to your father.

277
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:14,927
If your father didn't save my life…

278
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:17,471
you would've died long ago.

279
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:20,516
That's why you should be careful, Raul.

280
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:24,228
All debts of gratitude have their limits.

281
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:28,482
Get him out of here.

282
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,822
[Emilia] Raul? What happened?

283
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:37,449
What happened?

284
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:41,161
[tense music playing]

285
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:53,132
I'm sorry if…

286
00:18:54,424 --> 00:18:55,968
if I made you worry.

287
00:18:57,427 --> 00:18:58,929
Forget that, Diego.

288
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:02,307
What's important is you're home.

289
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:12,317
I just couldn't accept
that my real mother is gone.

290
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,655
I didn't even get to know her.

291
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:21,118
[sniffles]

292
00:19:24,872 --> 00:19:26,832
I want to find her parents. My relatives.

293
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:33,797
My biological relatives. Is that okay?

294
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:38,010
We'll help you find them, then.

295
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:41,388
Thank you.

296
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:56,361
-Have something to drink.
-Thank you.

297
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:10,542
Are you Rosa's son?

298
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:14,588
My grandson!

299
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:27,517
You have her eyes.

300
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:34,233
When you were still a baby,
she'd always read you books.

301
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:39,321
Your mother was intelligent,
always at the top of her class.

302
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,907
She had high hopes.

303
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:47,371
But she was a fool in love.
She went against an Ardiente.

304
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:50,040
[somber music playing]

305
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:58,840
We told her to leave your father.

306
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:01,677
But she loved him too much.

307
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:03,971
She didn't leave him until the very end.

308
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:08,600
Why did you stay silent?

309
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:11,895
Why didn't you do anything?

310
00:21:12,479 --> 00:21:14,856
We knew what the Ardientes
were capable of.

311
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:17,484
We have loved ones to protect…

312
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:20,445
and we didn't want to end up
like your mother.

313
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:26,743
Take these. These are Rosa's things.

314
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:34,376
It will help us all heal.

315
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:46,805
That's Rosario. Your mother.

316
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:52,352
[somber music playing]

317
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:25,218
Mom, the Ardientes can't go
against me because they need me.

318
00:22:25,927 --> 00:22:28,847
They need my money for their campaign.

319
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:33,435
Lily, you won't know for sure.
They're just using you.

320
00:22:33,518 --> 00:22:34,728
[laughs]

321
00:22:34,811 --> 00:22:37,898
-We're using each other, Mom.
-Each other?

322
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:40,942
Lily, I don't remember teaching you that!

323
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:42,861
Mom, I'm sorry.

324
00:22:42,944 --> 00:22:45,405
It's just that the Ardientes
love to play dirty.

325
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:49,326
If you don't bare your fangs,
they'll eat you alive.

326
00:22:50,118 --> 00:22:53,997
Ivy, do you want me to
contact Noel, Arthur, and Tonio?

327
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:58,376
Yes, please. As soon as possible.

328
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:00,670
We need them right away.

329
00:23:02,964 --> 00:23:04,007
Lily.

330
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,301
Who are they?

331
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:09,179
[tense music playing]

332
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:28,115
<i>I'm doing everything, Raul.</i>
<i>But why won't you still love me?</i>

333
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:38,708
Camia… Camia…

334
00:23:39,334 --> 00:23:40,544
[grunts]

335
00:23:40,627 --> 00:23:42,045
Camia again?

336
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:45,257
Camia, is it?

337
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,342
Till now.

338
00:23:50,345 --> 00:23:51,346
[door slams shut]

339
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:57,144
We need them, Mom. All three of them.

340
00:23:57,227 --> 00:24:00,522
They're the ones who'll testify
against the Ardientes.

341
00:24:04,442 --> 00:24:08,196
One of them is Arthur Dela Peña.

342
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:11,825
He used to work with Dad.
Do you remember him?

343
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:17,956
He's the one who saw
how Raul harassed you at school.

344
00:24:18,665 --> 00:24:21,209
<i>Let me go! Let me go!</i>

345
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,294
[pot breaks]

346
00:24:27,966 --> 00:24:32,179
He was also the one who Emilia
ordered to poison Dad.

347
00:24:32,262 --> 00:24:34,848
That's the reason why Dad died.

348
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:37,642
And then we have Emmanuel Condez.

349
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:41,313
He worked as a gravedigger
for the Ardientes.

350
00:24:41,938 --> 00:24:47,194
Raul ordered him to replace
your body with another one

351
00:24:48,445 --> 00:24:50,614
<i>to make us all believe you were dead.</i>

352
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:57,829
And Antonio Vidal.

353
00:24:57,913 --> 00:25:00,999
[tense music playing]

354
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,627
He was Emilia's former bodyguard.

355
00:25:09,299 --> 00:25:11,468
He was the one who tried to kill you…

356
00:25:13,803 --> 00:25:16,181
and buried you alive.

357
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:20,602
<i>-Go on. Get out of here.</i>
<i>-Hey!</i>

358
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:24,940
<i>-Lily… Run!</i>
<i>-Get off me!</i>

359
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:29,069
<i>No! </i>[grunts]

360
00:25:33,448 --> 00:25:34,491
Lily, dear.

361
00:25:34,574 --> 00:25:38,703
Mom. Don't worry.
You don't have to see them.

362
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:41,164
I'll take care of everything.
I'll talk to them alone.

363
00:25:41,248 --> 00:25:42,457
No.

364
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:45,085
I want to see Tonio.

365
00:25:49,422 --> 00:25:50,924
-Lily.
-But Mom…

366
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:55,470
I want to see the man who ruined my life.

367
00:26:16,032 --> 00:26:18,702
-[Camia] <i>Who are you?</i>
-[Tonio] <i>Don't be scared.</i>

368
00:26:18,785 --> 00:26:22,622
[Camia] <i>Why? Don't come any closer.</i>

369
00:26:23,415 --> 00:26:25,041
<i>We're going to have fun.</i>

370
00:26:26,793 --> 00:26:28,211
<i>We'll play a game.</i>

371
00:26:31,756 --> 00:26:33,300
[Camia crying]

372
00:26:33,383 --> 00:26:39,931
[Camia] <i>No! Stay away from me! No!</i>

373
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:45,937
[tense music playing]

374
00:26:58,408 --> 00:26:59,951
Forgive me.

375
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:03,121
Please forgive me.

376
00:27:07,625 --> 00:27:09,919
I'm sorry for what I did to you.

377
00:27:11,921 --> 00:27:16,343
Please forgive me.
I'm so sorry. Forgive me.

378
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:35,445
[soft music playing]

379
00:28:04,224 --> 00:28:05,892
Why did you do that to me?

380
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:11,648
I used to be one of
the Ardientes' most trusted men.

381
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:16,611
If you worked for them,
you were above the law.

382
00:28:17,695 --> 00:28:19,531
I was drunk with power.

383
00:28:21,199 --> 00:28:22,492
But not a single day passed by

384
00:28:22,575 --> 00:28:24,661
that I wasn't tormented by my conscience.

385
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:28,248
I have a wife now.

386
00:28:29,249 --> 00:28:30,583
And a daughter too.

387
00:28:31,835 --> 00:28:35,213
I would die if what I did to you
happened to them.

388
00:28:37,924 --> 00:28:39,050
Please forgive me.

389
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:43,722
[soft music playing]

390
00:28:52,313 --> 00:28:53,940
May God have mercy on you.

391
00:28:54,190 --> 00:28:58,486
[pensive music playing]

392
00:29:12,542 --> 00:29:15,795
[pensive music playing]

393
00:29:38,693 --> 00:29:40,278
[Raul] <i>You can't see her because…</i>

394
00:29:41,404 --> 00:29:44,741
<i>your mother's gone. Emilia had her killed.</i>

395
00:29:44,908 --> 00:29:45,700
<i>And besides… You know?</i>

396
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,660
<i>She deserves it. Your mom was a slut.</i>

397
00:29:47,827 --> 00:29:48,828
<i>-You murderer!</i>
<i>-Sir!</i>

398
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:49,746
[screams]

399
00:29:49,829 --> 00:29:51,623
[Arnaldo] <i>You ungrateful bastard!</i>

400
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:53,917
<i>This family raised you,</i>
<i>and this is how you repay us?!</i>

401
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,377
-<i>You're all animals!</i>
-[Julio] <i>Now, drive!</i>

402
00:30:27,742 --> 00:30:28,743
Ma'am?

403
00:30:33,540 --> 00:30:34,749
It's fine. You may go now.

404
00:30:36,751 --> 00:30:37,752
Diego.

405
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:43,758
What happened to you?

406
00:30:44,717 --> 00:30:45,844
Ivy, you were right.

407
00:30:48,012 --> 00:30:50,306
Everything you said
about the Ardientes is true.

408
00:30:52,767 --> 00:30:57,647
What your parents and my father said.

409
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:01,609
What are you talking about?

410
00:31:04,028 --> 00:31:05,947
Ivy, I'm not a real Ardiente.

411
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:08,950
I'm Raul's illegitimate son.

412
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:14,414
Emilia had my mother killed.

413
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:17,083
Like what she did to your parents.

414
00:31:19,627 --> 00:31:21,254
I thought they would change.

415
00:31:21,671 --> 00:31:24,465
But change isn't in their vocabulary.

416
00:31:26,968 --> 00:31:31,014
Ivy, we have the same goal now.
And that's to destroy them.

417
00:31:32,974 --> 00:31:33,892
Ivy, help me.

418
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:35,977
Come with me,
and let's take them to court.

419
00:31:38,146 --> 00:31:40,356
Help you take them to court?

420
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:44,819
What if I told you, Diego,
that the right punishment

421
00:31:44,903 --> 00:31:47,655
for the Ardientes
isn't written in the law?

422
00:31:47,989 --> 00:31:52,493
So I'll take it into my own
hands and deal with them myself.

423
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:54,412
[tense music playing]

424
00:32:06,633 --> 00:32:11,971
I'm sorry, my children.
We can't open the cooperative…

425
00:32:12,722 --> 00:32:16,100
until you settle things
with Governor Alvarez.

426
00:32:17,435 --> 00:32:23,107
But don't worry. I'm taking
measures to solve this problem.

427
00:32:23,483 --> 00:32:27,612
But when will that happen?
Our food supply is running out.

428
00:32:28,363 --> 00:32:30,698
The governor should return
what he stole from us.

429
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:33,368
That was from our blood, sweat, and tears.

430
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:38,122
Just have faith in me. Remember this.

431
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:42,543
A father never wants
to see his children suffer.

432
00:32:43,544 --> 00:32:48,841
All I ask of you is
your understanding and patience.

433
00:32:49,384 --> 00:32:50,927
I'll fix this.

434
00:32:52,345 --> 00:32:54,681
But I also need your help.

435
00:32:55,807 --> 00:32:57,892
Because I can't do this alone.

436
00:32:58,726 --> 00:33:02,855
If you will help me, then I can help you.

437
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:05,942
[tense music playing]

438
00:33:25,461 --> 00:33:28,297
Mister Fernan! Where are you going?

439
00:33:29,298 --> 00:33:30,633
It's none of your business, Diego.

440
00:33:34,345 --> 00:33:35,471
I'll go with you.

441
00:33:43,396 --> 00:33:44,689
Ivy, the attorney's here.

442
00:33:46,441 --> 00:33:48,818
-Good morning, Attorney.
-Good morning, Miss Aguas.

443
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:52,947
Meet my biological mother,
Miss Camia Cruz.

444
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:55,950
-Good morning, Attorney.
-Your mother?

445
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:58,536
It seems like we have a lot
to talk about, Miss Aguas.

446
00:33:58,661 --> 00:34:01,414
Yes, we do. Join us for breakfast.

447
00:34:01,622 --> 00:34:05,001
Well, if you want to put
the Ardientes behind bars,

448
00:34:05,293 --> 00:34:09,297
you should tell me everything.
I want all the juicy details.

449
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:11,299
[tense music playing]

450
00:34:11,382 --> 00:34:16,345
Attorney. The Ardientes have
so much influence and power.

451
00:34:17,346 --> 00:34:19,932
How can we take them down?

452
00:34:20,224 --> 00:34:21,642
They've gained power and influence

453
00:34:21,726 --> 00:34:24,103
because their people defend them
with their lives.

454
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:27,398
Turn their people against them,
and they'll be powerless.

455
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:38,284
[Fernan] Stop right here.

456
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:40,078
[Diego] Mr. Fernan,
are you sure it's here?

457
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:41,204
Yes.

458
00:34:41,370 --> 00:34:44,290
I'm sure the Ardientes are doing
some illegal activities here.

459
00:34:44,665 --> 00:34:45,708
Come on, let's go.

460
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:52,673
Hey. Emilio.

461
00:34:52,965 --> 00:34:58,096
Good evening! How are you?
I'm glad you could come visit.

462
00:34:58,179 --> 00:35:01,057
-Mayor.
-Governor's here.

463
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:02,642
How are you?

464
00:35:03,518 --> 00:35:05,478
Hey, Congressman. I'm glad you're here.

465
00:35:05,561 --> 00:35:08,856
-Well, I had some spare time.
-Governor.

466
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:11,567
Business is doing great, isn't it?

467
00:35:11,651 --> 00:35:14,821
-It really is.
-There are many players.

468
00:35:18,491 --> 00:35:19,575
[quietly] Diego!

469
00:35:23,287 --> 00:35:25,706
Mister Fernan, hang on.
Watch out for the guards.

470
00:35:25,790 --> 00:35:26,916
Wait. Hold on.

471
00:35:28,709 --> 00:35:30,586
Hang on! Careful. Someone's coming.

472
00:35:31,504 --> 00:35:33,506
[suspenseful music playing]

473
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:42,140
Do you know them?

474
00:35:45,268 --> 00:35:46,769
Those are Grandpa's men!

475
00:35:47,228 --> 00:35:48,938
It looks like they're bringing money.

476
00:35:50,231 --> 00:35:52,650
-Let's go check it out.
-Be careful.

477
00:35:55,945 --> 00:35:59,282
How about our income?

478
00:36:00,408 --> 00:36:02,243
-Olan?
-We're earning well.

479
00:36:06,831 --> 00:36:09,083
-How well?
-Enough to retire if we want to.

480
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:12,670
-That's good to hear.
-Thank you.

481
00:36:35,943 --> 00:36:38,362
Here he comes. Stay down.

482
00:36:41,157 --> 00:36:42,867
[whispering] Hide. Go. Go. Let's go.

483
00:36:48,497 --> 00:36:49,665
Let's go.

484
00:36:52,376 --> 00:36:54,337
Hey! Where are you going?

485
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:57,673
Well? You're spying on us, aren't you?

486
00:36:57,757 --> 00:36:58,758
-No!
-Really?

487
00:36:58,841 --> 00:36:59,759
-No.
-No, sir.

488
00:36:59,842 --> 00:37:02,178
All right. Come with me. Go on!

489
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:04,472
Come on!

490
00:37:06,557 --> 00:37:07,516
[gunshot]

491
00:37:07,600 --> 00:37:10,061
[tense music playing]

492
00:37:13,606 --> 00:37:15,233
-Come on!
-Let's go, Mister Fernan!

493
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:16,359
Move it!

494
00:37:16,567 --> 00:37:18,527
Hey. Find out what that was.

495
00:37:19,737 --> 00:37:23,741
Sit down. Please, continue.
Don't mind that.

496
00:37:23,824 --> 00:37:26,619
Someone must be celebrating his birthday

497
00:37:26,702 --> 00:37:28,746
with a little too much fun.

498
00:37:29,497 --> 00:37:31,749
Enjoy yourselves.
Please, continue. Keep playing.

499
00:37:38,714 --> 00:37:39,924
[Fernan] Hurry! Hurry!

500
00:37:44,387 --> 00:37:45,763
What happened here?

501
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,308
Hey!

502
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:52,478
Mister Fernan, let's go!

503
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:58,067
[Diego] Hurry!

504
00:38:00,027 --> 00:38:01,946
-Go! Hurry!
-Go! Go! Hurry!

505
00:38:02,780 --> 00:38:04,824
-Hurry up! Take cover! Duck!
-I knew it!

506
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:13,708
Congressman, we didn't catch them.

507
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:16,168
-How many were they?
-Two.

508
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:19,088
-Did you recognize any of them?
-No, sir. It was too dark.

509
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:22,133
I thought you sorted out
these problems, Governor.

510
00:38:22,216 --> 00:38:24,176
Why are the police still spying on us?

511
00:38:26,220 --> 00:38:28,055
It's impossible those were the police.

512
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:29,682
I spoke to the chief already.

513
00:38:29,807 --> 00:38:31,475
If they weren't police,
then who were they?

514
00:38:33,477 --> 00:38:35,354
Uh, Congressman,

515
00:38:35,438 --> 00:38:39,525
I think we should stop
the operations just to be safe.

516
00:38:39,650 --> 00:38:40,693
[scoffs]

517
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:43,195
What are you talking about, William?

518
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:44,780
Use your brain.

519
00:38:45,614 --> 00:38:46,741
Think about it.

520
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:49,910
If we're going to close down
this gambling den,

521
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:53,706
what will those people think?

522
00:38:55,791 --> 00:38:58,044
[Fernan] Diego and I saw the congressman.

523
00:38:58,544 --> 00:39:01,255
He's running the gambling den
in this town.

524
00:39:02,298 --> 00:39:04,300
We'll report them to the police.

525
00:39:04,508 --> 00:39:06,552
What can the police do?

526
00:39:06,844 --> 00:39:08,971
The congressman will just silence them.

527
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:11,849
The police are wrapped around my finger.

528
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:16,228
I control the information
that goes out to the media.

529
00:39:17,104 --> 00:39:19,565
If there are spies out there…

530
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,819
I dare them to reveal themselves.

531
00:39:24,195 --> 00:39:26,697
But Mister Fernan, what else can we do?

532
00:39:26,989 --> 00:39:29,033
The Ardientes stole from us.

533
00:39:29,658 --> 00:39:33,120
So, we aren't going to let them
get any money

534
00:39:33,204 --> 00:39:35,414
from that gambling den.

535
00:39:36,916 --> 00:39:38,626
We'll form a group.

536
00:39:39,585 --> 00:39:41,754
We'll take back from the Ardientes

537
00:39:41,837 --> 00:39:44,256
what's rightfully ours.

538
00:39:45,132 --> 00:39:47,009
Let's see how tough they are.

539
00:39:47,968 --> 00:39:49,970
Why did they even think
they could challenge us?

540
00:39:52,681 --> 00:39:53,724
Mister Fernan.

541
00:39:54,308 --> 00:39:57,395
Mister Fernan, don't do that.
You'll put everyone in danger!

542
00:39:57,603 --> 00:39:59,063
I'm not forcing anyone.

543
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:02,983
Join me if you want to seek
revenge on the Ardientes.

544
00:40:03,734 --> 00:40:06,946
And if you don't want to,
then stay out of this.

545
00:40:07,863 --> 00:40:09,448
I'll join you, Mister Fernan.

546
00:40:09,990 --> 00:40:11,784
-We'll join you.
-Thank you. Thank you.

547
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:14,120
-Me too, Mister Fernan.
-Me too. I'll join you.

548
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:15,621
-Thank you.
-Mister Fernan, I'll join you.

549
00:40:15,704 --> 00:40:17,540
I agree with you. Diego?

550
00:40:17,623 --> 00:40:20,084
[suspenseful music playing]

551
00:40:30,553 --> 00:40:31,512
Let's go there.

552
00:40:31,595 --> 00:40:34,265
[tense music playing]

553
00:40:42,189 --> 00:40:44,024
Attorney, why are they here?

554
00:40:44,483 --> 00:40:48,571
<i>We're here to expose</i>
<i>the corruption, lies, crimes,</i>

555
00:40:48,654 --> 00:40:52,241
<i>and mass murders committed</i>
<i>by Congressman Julio Ardiente,</i>

556
00:40:52,324 --> 00:40:54,618
<i>his daughter,</i>
<i>former governor Emilia Torillo,</i>

557
00:40:54,702 --> 00:40:57,997
<i>and her husband, Raul Torillo.</i>
<i>We have enough evidence and…</i>

558
00:40:58,080 --> 00:41:02,460
eyewitnesses to prove the crimes
the aforementioned people

559
00:41:02,543 --> 00:41:05,463
have committed within
the decade they were in office.

560
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:06,755
Are they gonna be ousted…

561
00:41:06,839 --> 00:41:08,174
-from power?
-Thank you very much.

562
00:41:08,757 --> 00:41:11,677
[tense music playing]

563
00:41:14,638 --> 00:41:17,141
<i>I was Governor Emilia's former bodyguard.</i>

564
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:22,271
<i>She asked me to kill a lot</i>
<i>of people, including…</i>

565
00:41:24,648 --> 00:41:25,649
<i>Camia Cruz.</i>

566
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:29,737
<i>She asked me to kill her out of jealousy.</i>

567
00:41:29,987 --> 00:41:32,740
[tense music playing]

568
00:41:44,376 --> 00:41:46,712
<i>I'm here to clear my conscience.</i>

569
00:41:47,296 --> 00:41:51,842
<i>I witnessed how Mr. Raul Torillo</i>
<i>harassed Camia Cruz.</i>

570
00:41:52,593 --> 00:41:58,557
<i>And also, how Emilia poisoned</i>
<i>Attorney Dante Cruz.</i>

571
00:42:02,269 --> 00:42:04,647
It's time for the people to know about

572
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:06,440
<i>all the evil and monstrous deeds</i>

573
00:42:06,524 --> 00:42:08,192
<i>the Ardientes have done.</i>

574
00:42:09,235 --> 00:42:11,820
<i>This is to give justice to all the people</i>

575
00:42:11,904 --> 00:42:13,781
<i>that have fallen victim</i>
<i>to them over the years.</i>

576
00:42:14,740 --> 00:42:16,951
Attorney, what can you say
to the Ardientes?

577
00:42:17,910 --> 00:42:19,328
<i>We're coming for all of you.</i>

578
00:42:19,411 --> 00:42:21,705
[dramatic music playing]

579
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:40,849
-No!
-Do you know those witnesses?

580
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:44,353
One of them claims
he was your former bodyguard.

581
00:42:44,436 --> 00:42:46,105
They know a lot about you.

582
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:48,691
I already asked my staff
to track him, Auntie.

583
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:50,943
But my question is, who's behind this?

584
00:42:51,777 --> 00:42:54,196
Your family has a lot of political rivals.

585
00:42:55,322 --> 00:42:59,410
It might be another party,
a businessman you crossed, or…

586
00:43:00,744 --> 00:43:01,745
Or what?

587
00:43:03,122 --> 00:43:04,123
Camia Cruz.

588
00:43:05,499 --> 00:43:08,335
Camia Cruz? Camia…

589
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:10,045
-Think about it.
-Camia.

590
00:43:10,129 --> 00:43:12,965
Of all the things they could
accuse your family of,

591
00:43:14,008 --> 00:43:18,887
they focused on Camia Cruz
and how you killed her husband.

592
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:21,807
If Camia Cruz were still alive,

593
00:43:21,890 --> 00:43:23,976
she would most likely come for you.

594
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:27,980
[ominous music playing]

595
00:43:28,063 --> 00:43:31,900
But what's bothering me is your
father's not doing anything.

596
00:43:32,735 --> 00:43:35,029
Aren't we supposed to be
doing damage control?

597
00:43:35,112 --> 00:43:37,615
Auntie, he probably hasn't
heard about this yet.

598
00:43:39,074 --> 00:43:41,410
Julio's silence is unnerving.

599
00:43:42,077 --> 00:43:44,663
You're the main suspect in this exposé.

600
00:43:45,581 --> 00:43:47,583
Your father would most likely rat you out

601
00:43:47,666 --> 00:43:49,043
just to save his ass.

602
00:43:49,293 --> 00:43:51,503
So, you really have to know
what's going on, Emilia.

603
00:43:56,550 --> 00:43:57,885
-Diego!
-Nimfa?

604
00:43:57,968 --> 00:44:01,180
Diego! Diego, it's Dad. I heard him.

605
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:04,391
They're going to attack
the congressman's gambling den!

606
00:44:04,767 --> 00:44:07,353
-What?
-Diego, I'm worried about Dad!

607
00:44:07,436 --> 00:44:08,729
He might get himself killed.

608
00:44:08,854 --> 00:44:10,105
Nimfa, listen to me.

609
00:44:10,272 --> 00:44:12,274
No one else should know about this.

610
00:44:12,358 --> 00:44:14,068
If the Ardientes find out
that Mister Fernan

611
00:44:14,151 --> 00:44:15,402
is going against them,

612
00:44:15,486 --> 00:44:17,488
your father's life will be at risk.

613
00:44:18,197 --> 00:44:20,908
But don't worry. I'll go after them.

614
00:44:36,590 --> 00:44:39,551
Come with me.
The three of you stay up here.

615
00:44:39,635 --> 00:44:41,720
If someone comes, knock them out!

616
00:44:41,804 --> 00:44:45,349
[suspenseful music playing]

617
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:53,774
Hey!

618
00:44:56,527 --> 00:44:58,404
-Hurry, hurry.
-Where are you going?!

619
00:44:58,487 --> 00:44:59,488
Drop your weapons!

620
00:44:59,571 --> 00:45:01,865
-Go ahead and shoot!
-Drop your gun!

621
00:45:03,075 --> 00:45:05,285
Hand me your gun. Hand it over.

622
00:45:05,369 --> 00:45:06,495
[grunts]

623
00:45:06,995 --> 00:45:09,832
Go, go! Keep an eye on him.

624
00:45:10,457 --> 00:45:11,708
We'll leave them to you.

625
00:45:11,792 --> 00:45:12,918
You got him, Dolfo.

626
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:16,463
[grunts]

627
00:45:17,631 --> 00:45:21,468
[Fernan] Get down! Get down!
All of you, get down!

628
00:45:21,969 --> 00:45:24,847
[suspenseful music playing]

629
00:45:26,598 --> 00:45:28,058
Watch out!

630
00:45:28,142 --> 00:45:29,560
-[unintelligible]
-[grunts]

631
00:45:32,855 --> 00:45:35,232
Are you okay? Let's go!

632
00:45:36,859 --> 00:45:41,321
Give me that! You!
Fill this up! Fill it up!

633
00:45:44,700 --> 00:45:48,620
Don't move! Stay down! Hurry up!

634
00:45:48,704 --> 00:45:50,747
Hey, stay down! I said stay down!

635
00:45:55,961 --> 00:45:57,129
Let's go!

636
00:46:03,135 --> 00:46:06,972
[suspenseful music playing]

637
00:46:12,186 --> 00:46:14,188
[reporter] <i>Is there any truth</i>
<i>to those accusations?</i>

638
00:46:14,271 --> 00:46:17,524
<i>-You shameless thieves!</i>
<i>-Hey! Ouch!</i>

639
00:46:17,608 --> 00:46:21,320
<i>Whoever's spreading rumors</i>
<i>about our family, face us!</i>

640
00:46:21,403 --> 00:46:25,324
<i>That Camia Cruz is becoming</i>
<i>a problem. Is she even real?</i>

641
00:46:25,407 --> 00:46:27,910
<i>She is real. She is a threat.</i>

642
00:46:27,993 --> 00:46:29,912
<i>She's not the only one behind this.</i>

643
00:46:29,995 --> 00:46:31,955
<i>Someone big is backing her up.</i>

644
00:46:32,039 --> 00:46:32,831
<i>Who could that be?</i>

645
00:46:32,915 --> 00:46:34,875
<i>Could it be her darned daughter?</i>

646
00:46:34,958 --> 00:46:38,879
<i>Do you know whom I'm suspecting?</i>
<i>Miss Aguas.</i>

647
00:46:38,962 --> 00:46:40,714
<i>It's time for me to fight them head-on.</i>

648
00:46:40,797 --> 00:46:43,926
<i>If you want to face them, then I will too.</i>

649
00:46:45,344 --> 00:46:48,138
[theme music playing]
